    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Populate resumewise_prod row\n\nClick **Execute workflow** to upsert the `resumewise_prod` row in `cs_project_config`.\nMatches on `project_key` — idempotent, safe to re-run.\n41 real values set. Defaults applied: message_limit_threshold=7,\nclassification_confidence_threshold=0.995, hmac_key_id=n8n-prod.\n\nClosest-to-LoveStyle project so far: 2-letter language codes and double-underscore\nrefund slugs — NO language/slug remap needed.\n\n## FILL BEFORE RUNNING (env/secret values only you have)\n- payments_api_base_url\n- slack_automation_errors_channel_id\n- slack_dev_error_channel_id\n- classification_model_id\n\n## OPEN DECISIONS (currently left at 0 — tell me to fill if you want them)\n- macro_account_deletion_id — RW has \"How to Delete My Account\" (27784313141138), but it's a\n  MANUAL how-to, not an automation macro. Left empty per the Mindspree precedent. Fill if wanted.\n- refund_macro_rejection_alt_id — only ONE rejection-automation macro exists. Closest alt is\n  \"Refund: Rejection - Final Answer\" (26546904288274), a manual escalation reply. Left empty.\n- refund_macro_no_upsell_to_refund_id — no matching macro in RW. Empty.\n\n## Left at 0 by rule / absence\n- ticket_custom_status_chatbot_automated_id — LoveStyle-only column, skipped.\n- ticket_field_chatbot_classification_id — no chatbot-classification field in RW.\n- ticket_field_contact_form_classification_id — no contact-form field in RW.\n\n## Notes (no action needed on the row)\n- Category refund slugs are DOUBLE underscore, upsell is SINGULAR (\"refund__upsell\") —\n  matches LoveStyle, deliberately different from Mindspree/MyImage. Do not \"normalize\".\n- Cancellation slugs are TRIPLE underscore (\"cancellation___subscription\") — correct, space in name.\n- Automation Classification field (37246518297490) option values are refund_auto / cancellation_auto\n  / other_auto — the classifier->field-write mapping must target these (template logic, not this row).\n- Allow Automation (37246467541138): _yes_ / _no_. Fail-open: block only on explicit _no_.\n- macro_cancellation_failed_payment_id resolved cleanly here (37246138242194, \"Failed Payment - Automation\").\n\n## After running\nVerify the row in the data table view, then archive this workflow.",
        "height": 900,
        "width": 760,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "1aabf02e-cca2-4182-93a7-4a17a22214ff",
      "name": "How to use",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
